+### Compound Format
+
+Use `compound` to get multiple units, largest first. Zero parts are skipped, the smallest unit is seconds (leftover milliseconds are dropped) and the largest is days. It takes precedence over `long`.
+
+```ts
+ms(5400000, { compound: true })       // "1h 30m"
+ms(-5400000, { compound: true })      // "-1h 30m"
+ms(90061000, { compound: true })      // "1d 1h 1m 1s"
+ms(3601999, { compound: true })       // "1h 1s"
+ms(999, { compound: true })           // "0s"
+```
+
 ### Input Formats (Units)
 
 ```ts
@@ -156,6 +168,8 @@ import { parse, format } from 'ms';
 parse('1h'); // 3600000
 
 format(2000); // "2s"
+
+format(5400000, { compound: true }); // "1h 30m"
 ```
 
 ### Enhanced Type Safety
